oo(t *testing.T) {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/cache_lifetime_test.go:362:func TestAPaddedTitleDoesNotKeepItsPaddingAlive(t *testing.T) {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/cache_lifetime_test.go:378:func TestTheOwnersBytesAreChargedToEachEntry(t *testing.T) {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/bounded_cache_test.go:22:func TestBoundedCacheEvictsByBytesNotEntries(t *testing.T) {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/bounded_cache_test.go:42:func TestBoundedCacheHoldsAnOwnerToItsBudget(t *testing.T) {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/bounded_cache_test.go:59:func TestBoundedCacheDoesNotRetainWhatExceedsTheBudget(t *testing.T) {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/bounded_cache_test.go:70:func TestBoundedCacheProducesOncePerKeyUnderConcurrentMisses(t *testing.T) {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/bounded_cache_test.go:109:func TestBoundedCacheDoesNotSerializeIndependentKeys(t *testing.T) {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/bounded_cache_test.go:134:func TestBoundedCacheWaiterCancellationLeavesTheProducerAndOthers(t *testing.T) {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/bounded_cache_test.go:175:func TestBoundedCacheDoesNotRememberAFailure(t *testing.T) {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/bounded_cache_test.go:190:func TestBoundedCacheExpiresByTTL(t *testing.T) {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/bounded_cache_test.go:202:func TestBoundedCacheSurvivesAlternatingOwnersUnderRace(t *testing.T) {\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md:50:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/cache_accounting_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md:51:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/cache_lifetime_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md:52:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/bounded_cache_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md:54:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/graph_cache_measure_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md:55:- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/cache_invalidation_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md:56:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/delivery_integrity_cache.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md:57:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/delivery_integrity_cache_test.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md:64:- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_spawn_cache.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md:70:### Delivery targets\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md:72:- capability:bounded-isolated-graph-caches module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/pose/delivery_integrity_cache.go\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md:74:### Approach and execution gates\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md:76:Executar após B15/B34. O cache atual lê conteúdo exato, guarda última entrada, permite decode de misses concorrentes e copia Nodes superficialmente; compactação schema2 ainda expande para grafo. Reusar a fundação done sem repetir seu ganho histórico. Definir API de vistas que não exponha coleções mutáveis compartilhadas, migração dos consumers e accounting/budgets com fixtures. A [proposta de runtime/cache](../adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md) e knowledge:adr-shared-worktree-runtime-review são prospectivos; completar todas estruturas/cache owners/consumers e paths antes do start. Não prometer zero-copy genérico nem bound de RAM apenas por LRU/TTL sem contabilizar pins/cópias. B35 só consome residência após qualificação; não dependência B35 para corrigir isolamento.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md:78:## 5. Decisions\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md:80:### Decision D1\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md:86:## 6. Validation\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md:88:### Strategy\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md:90:Fixtures sintéticas e o índice real do repositório como corpus de medição. Os casos V1-V8 foram executados; a evidência de cada requisito está no rastreio e na check `bounded-isolated-graph-caches-integration`.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md:92:### Deterministic checks\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md:96:### Requirement trace\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md:104:- R8 [satisfied] test:TestBoundedCacheSurvivesAlternatingOwnersUnderRace test:TestACancelledWaiterOnAGraphParseDoesNotAbandonTheOthers check:bounded-isolated-graph-caches-integration\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md:106:### Known gaps\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md:109:- The view's contract (do not modify or keep the graph) is documented and tested on the cache side, not enforced by the compiler.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md:113:## 7. Final Report\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md:115:### Delivered scope\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md:116:One bounded cache (bytes, global and per worktree, least recently used, optional expiry) carries the parsed delivery graph, the design-delta report and the test catalog; the paths of a commit are read by the governed capture, bounded in output (4 MiB) and in paths (100,000) and not cached, because every governed read is audited. A missed key is produced once however many callers ask, after reserving the bytes it expects to hold against global and per-worktree in-flight budgets, with a cap on productions and on waiters per key; a waiter that leaves does not disturb the producer or the others; a failure is never remembered; a value over its budget, or declared unretainable, is served and neither retained nor copied for retention; copies run outside the lock. Parsed graphs are keyed by engine, schema and the digest of the bytes, so identical bytes share an entry and nothing is served another worktree's graph. The test catalog is keyed by root and the digest of the validation matrix and expires after 30 seconds. The deep isolation is structural: a reflection test fills every slice, map and pointer of the graph and finds the references a copy shares with the original, which reproduced the aliasing the audit had not reproduced (the node attribute maps and the roadmap criteria refs) and fixed it. Read-only consumers can view the graph without a copy (`ViewDeliveryIntegrity`). Left out: moving every consumer to the view, RSS measurement, any persistent or cross-process cache, any global Git pool.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md:118:### Files and modules changed\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md:119:- pose-mcp/internal/pose (bounded_cache.go, delivery_integrity_cache.go, delivery_integrity.go, delegated_verdicts.go, design_delta.go, test_catalog.go, git_spawn_cache.go and their tests)\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md:120:- ADR shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime (amendment); the validation matrix gains `bounded-isolated-graph-caches-integration`\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md:122:### Validation executed\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md:126:### Residual risks\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md:127:- The clone a caller keeps is the caller's memory and is outside the budget; the view exists for readers that keep nothing. So are the inputs a caller read before asking the cache (the raw index bytes a waiter holds) and the clone being made for a caller: the cache charges what it keeps alive for itself, retained entries, productions, shared results until their last waiter copied them, and pinned entries. Bounding what callers allocate before and after the call is not done here; reading a smaller input is the follow-up below.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md:128:- An overloaded catalog cache is reported: lint-spec and the closeout gate fail with \"test references could not be verified\" instead of treating the missing catalog as an empty one; callers that only skip resolution keep the lenient form.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md:130:- The estimate of retained bytes errs high, so the cache holds less than its budget in practice.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md:133:### Follow-ups\n.pose/specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md:137:- [open] Bound what callers hold around the cache: read the delivery index in a bounded stream or by a size-gated admission before the bytes are allocated, and reserve the bytes of the clone a caller is about to receive. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2027-01-08)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
