{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"agent_message","text":"**Approved. No open findings.**\n\nThe registered cache integration tests passed under `-race`; `go vet ./internal/pose`, strict artifact-check, and strict surface-check also passed. Artifact-check reported provenance warnings; surface-check reported zero findings. The repository remains unchanged, and no attestation was recorded.\n\nApplied the POSE review workflow and backend-go, security, documentation-style, delivery-evidence, and knowledge-governance rules. Reviewed bundle `rvb-f4aedf9f53c7b470`; resolved plan digest `sha256:871b39b6d2500b369d6c17cb7c26e1f28c00e68ca3c5741038b2a3ae61a11fb9`.\n\nThe documented limits remain accepted: caller-owned inputs/copies are outside cache accounting, production reservations are estimates, catalog freshness permits 30 seconds, and RSS remains unmeasured. No whole-command speedup is inferred.\n\n`SD-64016923` maps to decision D1 and R1–R8: the ADR amendment defines cache budgets, coordination, isolation, freshness, ownership, and scoped Git reads. The shared cache implementation is proportionate; a global runtime or persistent cache would require separate justification.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [],\n  \"sweep\": \"Reviewed accounting, keys, isolation, failure handling and lifetimes across graph, design-delta and test-catalog caches, plus bounded uncached governed commit-path reads. Verified the prior documentation correction.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-b86d2cec5368a46f\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Verified isolation and cache coordination through code and race tests. Distinguished measured heap/allocation results from unmeasured RSS and command performance. Caller memory, estimated reservations, view ownership and catalog freshness are explicit accepted limits.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/bounded-isolated-graph-caches-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Independently reran the registered integration selection under -race. Publication, cancellation, waiter limits, admission, pinned entries and shared-result reservation tests passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-mcp-operation-results-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Mutable graph reads retain defensive-copy behavior. View access is additive. Catalog overload reaches CLI gates as incomplete verification; oversized commit inventories remain unknown.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/bounded-isolated-graph-caches-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Negative tests cover overload, failed production, cancellation, invalid graph data and excessive commit paths. Failures are not retained as successful absence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected Store, delegated-verdict, lint-spec and closeout consumers. Strict surface-check passed with one target, 191 results and zero findings.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/bounded-isolated-graph-caches-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Cache counters expose hits, misses, coalescing, eviction, failures and retained/reserved bytes. Returned overload context and incomplete-verification errors are bounded and actionable.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integrity-index-compaction-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Legacy and compact index decoding remains supported. Existing mutable reads remain isolated, with no new persistent format, daemon or Git pool.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/bounded-isolated-graph-caches-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Independent race-enabled integration tests and go vet passed. Sealed build:pose-mcp/go/build and unit:pose-mcp/go/test provide broader validation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-b86d2cec5368a46f\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Deep copies remove nested aliasing; read-only views avoid repeated whole-graph copies; byte accounting and per-key coordination address retention growth and duplicate production.\",\n      \"mappings\": [\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-64016923\",\n          \"basis\": \"D1\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The ADR amendment resolves R1-R8 through explicit ownership, budgets, keys, isolation, coordination, freshness and measurement boundaries.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reviewed operational docs, scaffold, ADR, changelog and spec. Commit paths are no longer described as cached; documented limits match runtime behavior.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"milestone-exit-gate-pose-shared-runtime-bounded-graph-caches\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/bounded-isolated-graph-caches-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Graph semantics, deep isolation, coordinated misses, owner/global accounting, pins and waiters have relevant tests. View allocation reduction is measured. Git remains scoped and governed; no authority cache is introduced. Applies within the spec's explicit memory and measurement limits.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/bounded-isolated-graph-caches-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Overload is reported rather than bypassing admission. Catalog-dependent gates report incomplete verification, and excessive commit inventories produce unknown coverage.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/bounded-isolated-graph-caches-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reviewed R1-R8 against implementation and requirement-trace tests. Independently executed the registered race-enabled selection; broader unit and integration evidence is sealed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-b86d2cec5368a46f\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Changes address bounded rebuildable caches, graph isolation, consumer error propagation and governed Git bounds. No resident runtime, persistent cache or global Git pool was added.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/git-and-dispatch-snapshot-integrity-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Cache hits do not establish current authority. Content/root keys preserve data boundaries, governed Git capture remains audited, and excessive inventories remain unknown.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-b86d2cec5368a46f\",\n      \"rationale\": \"One reusable cache implementation with defensive copies and limited view migration addresses the observed causes. Simpler entry-count or shallow-copy alternatives fail the requirements. New mutable dependencies, ownership changes or broader residency would require revisiting the design.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"check:pose artifact-check --spec pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed successfully, exit 0. Reported provenance warnings; no failing gate result.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-b86d2cec5368a46f\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed read-only assessment successfully. Its input digest matches the sealed structural evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Avoided repository-writing assessment refresh under the explicit unchanged-repository boundary; inspected component code and tests directly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Avoided repository-writing assessment refresh. Inspected provider-consumer boundaries directly and used sealed integration evidence plus the successful strict surface check.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Avoided repository-writing assessment refresh. Direct marker inspection found the intentional producer panic cleanup/rethrow; reservation, caller-memory and measurement debt already has owned spec follow-ups.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Diagnostic invocation exceeded 20 seconds. This completion-only gate must be rerun after POSE records and verifies the review; no attestation or closeout was written.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Diagnostic invocation exceeded 20 seconds. Final approval freshness verification belongs after POSE records this conclusion.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"check:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed successfully and applied the selected workflow and backend-go, security and documentation-style rules.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"surface-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed pose surface-check --spec pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches --strict: exit 0, one target, 191 results, zero findings. Supporting sealed reachability class: reachability:pose-mcp/go/delivery-reachability.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"build:pose-mcp/go/build\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reused supplied sealed validation to preserve the repository. Additional required classes: unit:pose-mcp/go/test; integration:pose-mcp/go/bounded-isolated-graph-caches-integration; e2e:pose-mcp/go/multi-repo-agent-installed-journey. Independently reran the cache integration selection under -race and go vet.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/bounded-isolated-graph-caches-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reused sealed module validation: build:pose-mcp/go/build; unit:pose-mcp/go/test; e2e:pose-mcp/go/multi-repo-agent-installed-journey. Independent registered cache integration selection under -race passed, as did go vet ./internal/pose.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
